### 8\. Internal DTD for customer details

File: `customer.dtd.xml`

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE customers [
    <!ELEMENT customers (customer+)>
    <!ELEMENT customer (id,name,email,city)>
    <!ELEMENT id (#PCDATA)>
    <!ELEMENT name (#PCDATA)>
    <!ELEMENT email (#PCDATA)>
    <!ELEMENT city (#PCDATA)>
]>
<customers>
    <customer>
        <id>101</id>
        <name>Arun</name>
        <email>arun@gmail.com</email>
        <city>Chennai</city>
    </customer>
</customers>
```

The DTD specifies that `customers` contains one or more `customer` elements. Each customer must contain `id`, `name`, `email`, and `city` in that order.

