```

Replace `root` and `password` with your own MySQL credentials. In modern Tomcat versions, servlet imports use `jakarta.servlet.*`; older Tomcat 9 labs generally use `javax.servlet.*`. The examples below use `javax.servlet.*` for compatibility with older college practical setups.

### 1\. Java program to connect to a database, store and retrieve information

File: `DatabaseDemo.java`

```java
import java.sql.*;

public class DatabaseDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Class.forName("com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver");

        Connection con = DriverManager.getConnection(
            "jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/webdb",
            "root", "password");

        Statement st = con.createStatement();

        st.executeUpdate(
            "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS student(" +
            "id INT PRIMARY KEY, name VARCHAR(30))");

        st.executeUpdate(
            "INSERT INTO student VALUES(1,'Arun') " +
            "ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE name='Arun'");

        ResultSet rs = st.executeQuery("SELECT * FROM student");

        while (rs.next()) {
            System.out.println(rs.getInt("id") + " " +
                               rs.getString("name"));
        }

        con.close();
    }
}
```

Output:

```text
1 Arun
```

